  "executive_briefing": "The cryptocurrency market is undergoing a structural realignment as the U.S. Senate approaches its upcoming vote on the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633). This landmark legislative push is redefining regulatory jurisdictions between the SEC and CFTC, creating a secure compliance runway that directly empowers native Bitcoin programmability and non-EVM smart contract execution. As developers capitalize on these native capabilities, Ethereum's historical smart contract monopoly faces formidable architectural competition. Simultaneously, institutional Bitcoin adoption is maturing away from speculative retail-driven ETF inflows into sophisticated, regulated treasury strategies and derivatives. To mitigate systemic vulnerabilities inherent in legacy custodial bridges, decentralized finance is rapidly pivoting toward trust-minimized, non-custodial cross-chain routing protocols that seamlessly unify fragmented BTC and EVM liquidity.",
